{% comment %}
  Our Story closing letter (Figma "06 Closing letter"): the page split into two equal halves, a photo on the
  left and a dark color1 panel on the right holding an eyebrow, two paragraphs and an italic sign-off.

  The photo is the same workshop shot the homepage heritage block uses (shopify://shop_images/heritage-archive.jpg,
  set in the template), so nothing is uploaded for it. The Figma suggests swapping it for a team or family
  photo so the two pages do not repeat; the picker is here for that.

  Below 750px the halves stack, photo above panel.

  Type: --font-size--2xs for the eyebrow, --font-paragraph--size for the two paragraphs, .h3 for the
  sign-off (28px, Lora, italic). The first paragraph can be set larger (24px pull-quote or 32px heading
  rung) with "Opening line size"; the default is body copy.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  Phones get their own sizes for the opening line and the sign-off ("... on phones" settings). Left on the
  desktop classes, the statement rendered at the h2 phone step (28) and the sign-off at h3 (28): the same
  size as every section title on the page, so the panel read louder than the headings around it. The
  ladder puts a pull quote at 24, which is the default; the sign-off steps down to 18 beneath it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  case section.settings.opening_size_mobile
    when 'body'
      assign open_mobile = 'var(--font-paragraph--size)'
    when 'heading'
      assign open_mobile = 'var(--font-h2--size)'
    else
      assign open_mobile = 'var(--font-h4--size)'
  endcase
  case section.settings.signoff_size_mobile
    when 'h4'
      assign signoff_mobile = 'var(--font-h4--size)'
    when 'h3'
      assign signoff_mobile = 'var(--font-h3--size)'
    else
      assign signoff_mobile = 'var(--font-h5--size)'
  endcase
-%}

<div
  class="story-letter{% if section.settings.image == blank and request.design_mode == false %} story-letter--no-photo{% endif %}"
  style="
    --sl-panel: {{ settings.color_palette.color1 }};
    --sl-eyebrow: {{ settings.color_palette.color7 }};
    --sl-ink: {{ settings.color_palette.background }};
    --sl-signoff: {{ settings.color_palette.color7 }};
    --sl-tile: {{ settings.color_palette.color9 }};
    --sl-soft: {{ settings.color_palette.color8 }};
    --sl-focus: {{ section.settings.focus_x }}%;
    --sl-height: {{ section.settings.desktop_height }}px;
    --sl-open-mobile: {{ open_mobile }};
    --sl-signoff-mobile: {{ signoff_mobile }};
  "
  data-testid="story-letter"
>
  {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
    <div class="story-letter__photo">
      {%- comment -%}
        `sizes` must describe the width the image is PAINTED at, not the width of its box. The box is
        taller than it is wide (50vw x 500px desktop, 4/3 mobile) while the photo is 16:9, so
        `object-fit: cover` scales it to cover the HEIGHT and crops the sides - the painted width comes
        out wider than the box. Desktop: a 720 x 500 box covers at 500px tall x 16/9 = ~889px painted,
        so 900px holds from 750px up to where 50vw overtakes it (1800px wide). Mobile: (100vw x 3/4) x
        16/9 = ~133vw. The desktop height is the "Desktop height" setting; at the default 500 these
        numbers hold, a taller row paints proportionally wider.

        The ladder runs to 2400 (the source's own width) so a 2x display has a candidate to reach for.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{
        section.settings.image
        | image_url: width: 2400
        | image_tag: widths: '720, 1080, 1440, 1600, 2048, 2400', sizes: '(min-width: 1800px) 50vw, (min-width: 750px) 900px, 134vw', alt: section.settings.image.alt, class: 'story-letter__img', loading: 'lazy'
      }}
    </div>
  {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
    <div class="story-letter__photo story-letter__photo--brief">
      <p class="story-letter__brief">Photo to come: a team or family photo, or the workshop shot from the homepage.</p>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="story-letter__panel">
    {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="story-letter__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      case section.settings.opening_size
        when 'heading'
          assign opening_class = 'story-letter__text h2'
        when 'quote'
          assign opening_class = 'story-letter__text h4'
        else
          assign opening_class = 'story-letter__text'
      endcase
    -%}
    {%- if section.settings.paragraph_1 != blank -%}
      <p class="{{ opening_class }} story-letter__opening">{{ section.settings.paragraph_1 }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.paragraph_2 != blank -%}
      <p class="story-letter__text">{{ section.settings.paragraph_2 }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.signoff != blank -%}
      <p class="h3 story-letter__signoff">{{ section.settings.signoff }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .story-letter {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .story-letter__photo {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .story-letter__img {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: var(--sl-focus) 50%;
  }

  .story-letter__photo--brief {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--sl-tile);
  }

  .story-letter__brief {
    max-width: 320px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size--sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--sl-soft);
  }

  .story-letter__panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 28px;
    padding: 64px 24px;
    background: var(--sl-panel);
  }

  .story-letter__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-subheading--family);
    font-weight: var(--font-subheading--weight);
    font-size: var(--font-size--2xs);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sl-eyebrow);
  }

  /* The opening line can carry .h4 or .h2 (see "Opening line size"). Those paint with
     `color: var(--color)` and own their size, so --color is set here as well as color. */
  .story-letter__text {
    --color: var(--sl-ink);

    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-paragraph--size);
    line-height: var(--line-height--body-loose);
    color: var(--sl-ink);
  }

  /* The type scale gives .h2 / .h4 a line height of 1, which lets a wrapped statement touch itself;
     doubled class to beat .h2.h2 / .h4.h4. */
  .story-letter__text.h2.h2,
  .story-letter__text.h4.h4 {
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  /* .h3 paints with `color: var(--color)`, so the colour goes in through --color. The italic is a second
     class deep because .h3.h3 (0,2,0) sets font-style from the type scale, which has no italic option. */
  .story-letter__signoff.story-letter__signoff {
    --color: var(--sl-signoff);

    margin: 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Phone sizes from the "... on phones" settings. `.story-letter` in front lifts these to (0,3,0) so they
     beat the type scale's .h2.h2 / .h3.h3 (0,2,0). */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .story-letter .story-letter__opening.story-letter__opening {
      font-size: var(--sl-open-mobile);
    }

    .story-letter .story-letter__signoff.story-letter__signoff {
      font-size: var(--sl-signoff-mobile);
    }
  }

  /* No photo and not in the editor: the panel takes the whole row. */
  .story-letter--no-photo .story-letter__panel {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .story-letter {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      min-height: var(--sl-height);
    }

    .story-letter__photo {
      aspect-ratio: auto;
    }

    .story-letter__panel {
      padding: 96px 112px 96px 96px;
    }

    .story-letter--no-photo {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Story closing letter",
  "class": "section-story-letter",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Photo",
      "info": "Left half. The template uses the workshop photo from the homepage."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "focus_x",
      "label": "Photo focus",
      "info": "Which part of the photo stays in view when it is cropped to the half. 0 is the left edge, 100 the right.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 58
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "desktop_height",
      "label": "Desktop height",
      "info": "Minimum height of the photo and panel row on desktop.",
      "min": 400,
      "max": 900,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 500
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Letter"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "SINCE 1974"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "paragraph_1",
      "label": "First paragraph",
      "default": "For over fifty years, we've made shoes for the people who keep Singapore running. Now we'd love to fit you too."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "opening_size",
      "label": "Opening line size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "body", "label": "Body copy (16px)" },
        { "value": "quote", "label": "Pull quote (24px)" },
        { "value": "heading", "label": "Heading (32px)" }
      ],
      "default": "body"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "opening_size_mobile",
      "label": "Opening line size on phones",
      "options": [
        { "value": "body", "label": "Body copy (16px)" },
        { "value": "quote", "label": "Pull quote (24px)" },
        { "value": "heading", "label": "Heading (28px)" }
      ],
      "default": "quote"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "paragraph_2",
      "label": "Second paragraph",
      "default": "Whether you stand through a twelve-hour shift or simply need a shoe with more room, come and see us."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "signoff",
      "label": "Sign-off",
      "default": "Fitted with care, since 1974."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "signoff_size_mobile",
      "label": "Sign-off size on phones",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h5", "label": "18px" },
        { "value": "h4", "label": "24px" },
        { "value": "h3", "label": "28px" }
      ],
      "default": "h5"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Story closing letter"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
